Semascope
Copyright 2026 Ryan Ballantyne and the Semascope contributors

This product includes software developed at The Apache Software Foundation
(https://www.apache.org/) when deployed with Apache Solr and Apache Tika.

Semascope is an independent, clean-room implementation. It was inspired by
Open Semantic Search (https://opensemanticsearch.org, GPL-3.0) but contains
none of its code, configuration, templates or documentation.

deploy/solr/configsets/documents/conf/ holds stop word, contraction and
stemmer-override lists (stopwords_*.txt, contractions_*.txt, stemdict_nl.txt)
copied unchanged from the lang/ folder of Apache Solr 10.0.0's _default
configset (Apache License 2.0). Several of them come, as their headers say, from
the Snowball project (https://snowballstem.org, BSD licence) and from Jacques
Savoy's CLEF lists (BSD licence); each file keeps its original notice.
